      "message": "Nit: I started to ask if this could be a sequence of makefile function calls, because I think that might be easier to read. Something like this.\n```\ncmd_json_list \u003d $(subst $(space),$(space)$(comma),$(sort $(1)))\n```\nI think `sort` would implicitly transform any newlines to spaces.\n\nBut this is also the kind of thing that could be tedious to get right.\n\nHow would you feel about passing `-E` to `sed` to use extended regexes and get rid of some of those backslashes? That might do a bit to make this easier to read.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "f3c3207b7828ffab12a975c486251ca0d3b9d616",
