      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, it might be nicer, but I don\u0027t think I can get Make to do this transformation, since make\u0027s text functions work on words/tokens between the space separators. I did try again, tho.\n\nCheckout these examples:\n\n```shell\n$(info $(subst  ,S,test inside quotes))\n# is interpreted equally to\n$(info $(subst ,S,test inside quotes))\n# is interpreted equally to\n$(info $(subst ,S,\"test inside quotes\"))\n# is interpreted equally to\nspace \u003d  \n$(info $(subst $(space),S,test inside quotes))\n# all of which just put a single S at the end of the the line\n```\n\nMaking `space \u003d \" \"` means that `subst` sees two words, `\"` and `\"`.\n\nI am very willing to change this to something that is more pleasant.\n\n---\n\nHmm, I would have thought that `strip` would have removed the trailing newline, too, but no such luck. Anyways, we don\u0027t want to sort the arg.\n\n---\n\n\u003e How would you feel about passing -E to sed to use extended regexes and get rid of some of those backslashes? That might do a bit to make this easier to read.\n\nThat\u0027s works! But, it still doesn\u0027t remove my double escaped quotes.",
      "parentUuid": "bd6c96be_fea7caaa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "f3c3207b7828ffab12a975c486251ca0d3b9d616",
